{
  "content": {
    "body": "A **knowledge** pebble is a shared CONTEXT document — free-form markdown\nthat describes a subsystem, an architecture, a convention, or a domain\nconcept, so agents / skills / rules can LOAD it as background instead of\nre-deriving it. It answers \"what you need to KNOW\" — not \"how to do X\" (a\nskill), \"who does it\" (an agent), or \"what must hold\" (a rule). The system\ndocs you are reading — including this one — ARE knowledge pebbles.\n\n## Pebble-level components\n\n- **name** — the topic (\"Auth subsystem\", \"Foresight multitenancy\").\n- **status** — AI-side lifecycle: Draft (`planned`) → Active (`verified`) →\n  Inactive (`deprecated`).\n- **description** — one-line summary of the topic (the recall hook).\n- **references** — knowledge may reference OTHER **knowledge** it builds on\n  and the spec pebbles it documents (models, structures, workflows, api).\n  Use references to point at the PEBBLES a doc is about. It does NOT\n  reference rules — rules are referenced only by skills and agents.\n- **resources** — YES (unlike rules/agents/skills). A knowledge doc often\n  describes REAL code — an architecture, a subsystem — so it links the\n  code files it documents via `link-code`; those are its investigation\n  entry points, found through the mapping feature (see mapping-reference).\n\n## Content component\n\n- **body** — the whole document, in markdown. That is the only content\n  field: knowledge is prose. Structure it with headings; cite file:line for\n  claims grounded in code; keep it truthful to what the code actually does.\n\nKnowledge is REFERENCED BY skills, agents and rules (as the context / the\nstandard they are grounded in).\n\n## Quick map — component → what's under it\n\n| Component | Under it |\n|---|---|\n| pebble.name | topic (string) |\n| pebble.status | Draft (planned) · Active (verified) · Inactive (deprecated) |\n| pebble.description | one-line recall hook |\n| references | other knowledge · pebbles it documents (NOT rules) |\n| resources | code links → the files/architecture it documents (allowed) |\n| content.body | the full markdown document |\n\n## Knowledge CLI — all knowledge operations live here\n\nContent kind is **text** (a single `body`). `content` is written WHOLE.\nFor a long, multiline body, build the JSON so the newlines are real — a\nheredoc piped through `jq` is the safe way; short bodies can be inline.\n\nCREATE (multiline body via heredoc + jq):\n\n    pebbles-cli create knowledge --title \"Auth subsystem\" --content \"$(jq -n --arg b \"$(cat <<'MD'\n    ## Overview\n\n    JWT is issued at /login and refreshed at /token; sessions live in Redis.\n\n    ## Key files\n\n    - app/Services/AuthService.php — token issue/refresh\n    - app/Http/Middleware/Authenticate.php — guard\n    MD\n    )\" '{kind:\"text\", body:$b}')\"\n\nCREATE (short inline body):\n\n    pebbles-cli create knowledge --title \"Cache policy\" --content '{\"kind\":\"text\",\"body\":\"Reads cache 5m in Redis; writes bust by tag. See CacheService.\"}'\n\nEDIT (append/rewrite — knowledge is NOT append-only like findings):\n\n    pebbles-cli update knowledge/auth-subsystem.pebble --patch \"$(jq -n --arg b \"$(cat <<'MD'\n    ## Overview\n    ...updated...\n    MD\n    )\" '{content:{kind:\"text\", body:$b}}')\"\n\nRESOURCES / references / status / inspect:\n\n    pebbles-cli link-code knowledge/auth-subsystem.pebble --file app/Services/AuthService.php --symbol AuthService\n    pebbles-cli set-status knowledge/auth-subsystem.pebble verified      # Active\n    pebbles-cli refs knowledge/auth-subsystem.pebble\n    pebbles-cli get knowledge/auth-subsystem.pebble\n    pebbles-cli set-status knowledge/auth-subsystem.pebble deprecated      # retire (no delete)\n\n## Related\n\nKnowledge is grounded via **resources** (see the resources sections of the\nmodel/structure/finding docs) and located through **mapping-reference**.",
    "kind": "text"
  },
  "createdAt": "2026-07-27T17:07:12.818Z",
  "description": "The component CATALOG of a Knowledge pebble (a shared CONTEXT document — free-form markdown describing a subsystem, architecture, convention or domain concept that agents/skills/rules load as background): its single body component, what it references, that it MAY carry resources (code links) since it often documents real code, and the full knowledge pebbles-cli usage. This very doc is a knowledge pebble. A DEFINITION reference skills point at.",
